      "category": "chemistry",
      "want": "J",
      "got": "J",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "Graham's law: v1/v2 = √(M2/M1). Let M1 = 4.005 g/mol (He). v1/v2 = 5.33, so M2/M1 = 5.33^2 ≈ 28.41. M2 = 4.005 × 28.41 ≈ 113.8 g/mol.\n(A) Ne: 20.19 → 5.03\n(B) CO2: 44.01 → 10.0\n(C) Ar: 39.95 → 9.98\n(D) CH4: 16.04 → 2.5\n(E) O2: 32.00 → 8.0\n(F) C5H12: 72.15 → 4.24\n(G) SO2: 64.06 → 6.33\n(H) N2: 28.01 → 7.07\n(I) H2O: 18.02 → 4.47\n(J) C8H18: 114.22 → 5.33\n\nM2 = 114.22 g/mol odpovídá C8H18.\n\nAnswer: (J)"
