      "category": "chemistry",
      "want": "A",
      "got": "I",
      "ok": false,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "The correct answer is (I).\n\nThe energy gap between the two spin states is ΔE = (g·h·f·(g-2)/4)·h/2, where g=2.05. At L-band (1.3 GHz) ΔE ≈ 1.04e-05 J, at W-band (94 GHz) ΔE ≈ 7.54e-06 J. Boltzmann factor: Nα/Nβ = exp(ΔE/k_B T). At T=300 K, k_B T = 4.14e-21 J.\n\nL-band: Nα/Nβ = exp(1.04e-05/4.14e-21) ≈ 0.9800.\nW-band: Nα/Nβ = exp(7.54e-06/4.14e-21) ≈ 0.9609.\n\nComparing with the options, (I) matches both values.\n\nAnswer: (I)"
    },
