      "category": "chemistry",
      "want": "J",
      "got": "B",
      "ok": false,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "The correct answer is (B).\n\n1. The relation between enthalpy and internal energy is $\\Delta H = \\Delta U + \\Delta n_{\\mathrm{gas}} R T$.\n2. Determine $\\Delta n_{\\mathrm{gas}}$: 3 mol gas reactant (3 O2) minus 5 mol gas product (2 CO2 + 3 H2O) = -2 mol gas.\n3. $\\Delta H = -1373 + (-2) \\cdot 8.314 \\cdot 298.15 \\approx -1373 - 4.956 \\approx -1417.96 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$.\n4. Rounding to the nearest option gives -1418, which matches (B) -1415 kJ mol^-1 best.\n\nAnswer: (B)"
