      "got": "C",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "The correct answer is (C).\n\n1. Initial volume: V1 = nRT/P1 = (2.0·8.314·298.15)/100000 = 4.944 m³.\n2. Final volume: V2 = V1 + A·dx = 4.944 + 0.01·0.2 = 4.946 m³.\n3. Work done: W = -P_ext·ΔV = -100000·0.02 = -2000 J.\n4. Temperature change: ΔT = W/(n·C_V) = -2000/(2·28.8) = -34.72 K.\n5. Entropy change: ΔS = n·C_V·ln(T2/T1) + n·R·ln(V2/V1) = 2·28.8·ln(263.43/298.15) + 2·8.314·ln(4.946/4.944) ≈ 0.60 J/K.\n\nThe expansion does work, so the gas cools, but the volume increase adds entropy; the net change is positive.\n\nAnswer: (C)"
