      "raw": "The correct answer is (B).\n\n1. Work done by the gas: W = P_ext·ΔV = 10000·(10.0·20·10^{-4}) = 20 J. Since the gas does work, W is negative in the convention ΔU = Q + W.\n2. Temperature change: ΔT = W/(n·C_V) = 20/(2·28.8) ≈ 0.3472 K.\n3. ΔU = n·C_V·ΔT = 2·28.8·0.3472 ≈ -60 J.\n\nThe work is negative because the system does work on the surroundings, and in an adiabatic process Q=0, so all energy change comes from W.\n\nAnswer: (B)"
