      "category": "chemistry",
      "want": "F",
      "got": "F",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "Coulomb's law: E = k·(q1·q2)/r, where r is the interionic distance, proportional to the sum of ionic radii. Larger ions mean larger r, so lower electrostatic attraction and lower lattice energy. Na+ is smaller than K+, so NaF has higher lattice energy than KCl. This trend is consistent with the data.\n\nAnswer: (F)"
