      "got": "I",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "Coulomb's law gives bond energy proportional to q1*q2/r. (a) Doubling q1 doubles the product q1*q2, so energy doubles. (b) Doubling both q1 and q2 quadruples the product, but this is the question's claim — let's re-evaluate. (c) Doubling r halves the denominator, so energy doubles. (d) Doubling both r1 and r2 (assuming r is the interatomic distance) doubles the denominator, halving the energy.\n\nWait, let's re-read the options carefully. Option B says (a) doubled, (b) same, (c) halved, (d) halved. Let's re-calculate: (a) q1*2/r → 2x; (b) (2q1)*(2q2)/r = 4q1q2/r → 4x; (c) q1*q2/(r/2) = 2q1q2/r → 2x; (d) q1*q2/(2r) = 0.5q1q2/r → 0.5x.\n\nOption B says (a) doubled, (b) same, (c) halved, (d) halved. This doesn't match my calculation for (b) and (c). Let's re-check the options. Option I: (a) doubled, (b) quadrupled, (c) halved, (d) quarter. This matches my calculation exactly.\n\nAnswer: (I)"
