      "category": "math",
      "want": "E",
      "got": "E",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "The dimension of the kernel is 2. The domain V has dimension 6 (2×3 = 6) and the codomain W has dimension 4. By the rank-nullity theorem, dim(V) = rank(T) + nullity(T). Since T is onto, rank(T) = dim(W) = 4. Thus nullity(T) = 6 − 4 = 2.\n\nAnswer: (E)"
