      "category": "math",
      "want": "G",
      "got": "A",
      "ok": false,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "The answer is (A).\n\nThe units digit of a power depends only on the units digit of the base. For 7^n, the units digits cycle every 4 powers: 7^1 ends in 7, 7^2 in 9, 7^3 in 3, 7^4 in 1, and then repeats. Since 25 mod 4 = 1, the units digit of 7^25 is the same as 7^1, which is 8.\n\nAnswer: (A)"
