      "id": "mmlu_math_7742",
      "category": "math",
      "want": "G",
      "got": "G",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "The area is 50. The legs are a = c·sin(45°) = 10·sin(45°) = 7.0711 and b = c·cos(45°) = 7.0711. Area = 0.5ab = 0.5·7.0711² = 25. A right triangle with a 45° angle is isosceles, so a=b. Area = 0.5·a² = 0.5·(c·sin 45°)² = 0.5·100·0.5 = 25.\n\nAnswer: (G)"
