      "category": "physics",
      "want": "B",
      "got": "C",
      "ok": false,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "The correct answer is (C).\n\nThe Andromeda galaxy (M31) is located approximately 2.537 million light-years from Earth, which is closest to 2.1 million light-years among the given options, though the exact value is 2.537. This distance is measured using Cepheid variables and other standard candles.\n\nAnswer: (C)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_physics_9048",
      "category": "physics",
      "want": "J",
      "got": "F",
      "ok": false,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "A meteor shower occurs when Earth passes through a cloud of debris left behind by a comet or asteroid. Comets, as they orbit the Sun, lose ice and dust due to sublimation, which gets left behind along their orbit. When Earth crosses this debris cloud, these particles enter the atmosphere at high speed and burn up, appearing as meteors. Option (F) correctly describes this mechanism. Option (J) is similar but refers to asteroids, which can also produce meteor showers, but the classic explanation usually cites cometary debris. Option (B) is also technically correct for asteroid-derived showers. Option (H) describes a single meteor, not a shower. Option (I) is space debris, not a meteor shower. Option (C) is incorrect. Option (D) is incorrect. Option (E) is incorrect. Option (G) is incorrect.\n\nAnswer: (F)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_physics_9049",
      "category": "physics",
      "want": "F",
      "got": "F",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "(F)\n\n1. Sunlight (mostly visible/UV) passes through the atmosphere and heats the surface.\n2. The surface re-emits infrared radiation.\n3. Greenhouse gases (CO2, CH4, H2O) absorb this infrared radiation and re-emit it in all directions, including back towards the surface.\n4. This traps heat in the lower atmosphere instead of letting it escape to space.\n5. Ozone absorbs UV, not infrared, and has little to do with the greenhouse effect.\n\nAnswer: (F)"
