      "want": "G",
      "got": "G",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "The correct answer is (B).\n\nThe illumination I is given by I/r², where I is the source intensity and r is the distance. I = 75/5² = 75/25 = 3 foot-candles. Wait, let me re-calculate: 75/25 = 3.\n\nRe-calculating: 75/25 = 3. Let me re-check the options.\n\n(A) 5, (B) 1, (C) 50, (D) 15, (E) 20, (F) 30, (G) 3, (H) 8, (I) 75, (J) 10.\n\nAh, 75/25 = 3. That's option (G). Let me re-read the question. 75 candlepower, 5 feet. I = 75/25 = 3.\n\nWait, I misread my own scratchpad. 75/25 is 3. Option (G) is 3.\n\nLet me re-calculate one more time: 75/25 = 3. Yes.\n\nAnswer: (G)"
