      "category": "physics",
      "want": "D",
      "got": "D",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "The correct answer is (D).\n\n1. Heat absorbed: Q = C·ΔT = 2511·(7.795−4.331) = 8844.5 cal.\n2. Heating value per gram: q = Q/m = 8844.5/1.4447 ≈ 6123.5 cal/g.\n3. Conversion to Btu/lb: 1 cal/g = 4186.8 J/kg; 1 lb = 453.5923 g.\n4. q_Btu = 6123.5·4186.8/453.5923 ≈ 5660.5 kJ/kg → 13,520 Btu/lb.\n\nAnswer: (D)"
