      "want": "A",
      "got": "B",
      "ok": false,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "The maximum kinetic energy of emitted electrons is E_max = hf - W0 = hc/λ - W0. Using h·c = 1240 eV·nm, E_max = 1240/0.390 - 1.90 = 3179.5 - 1.90 = 3177.6 eV. This is the maximum energy of the fastest electron.\n\nAnswer: (B)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_physics_9098",
      "category": "physics",
      "want": "A",
      "got": "B",
      "ok": false,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "The correct answer is (B).\n\nLet v_b be the boat's speed relative to water, v_c the current, and t1 the time upstream before turning. The bottle drifts downstream at speed v_c. The boat's speed upstream is v_b−v_c, downstream v_b+v_c.\n\n1) The bottle drifts x = 1 mile: t_total = x/v_c = 1/v_c.\n2) The boat travels upstream for t1, then downstream for t2 = t_total − t1.\n3) The distance the boat travels upstream is (v_b−v_c)t1, downstream (v_b+v_c)t2.\n4) The net downstream displacement of the boat relative to the drop point is (v_b+v_c)t2 − (v_b−v_c)t1 = x.\n5) Substituting t2 = 1/v_c − t1: (v_b+v_c)(1/v_c − t1) − (v_b−v_c)t1 = 1.\n6) Simplifying: v_b/v_c + 1 − (v_b+v_c)t1 − (v_b−v_c)t1 = 1 → v_b/v_c = 2v_b t1.\n7) Since t1 = 15 min = 0.25 h, v_b/v_c = 2v_b(0.25) = 0.5v_b.\n8) Dividing by v_b (assuming v_b ≠ 0): 1/v_c = 0.5 → v_c = 2.0 km/h.\n\nAnswer: (B)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_physics_9099",
      "category": "physics",
      "want": "A",
      "got": "A",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "The average speed is (B).\n\nLet the total distance be 2d. The first half takes t1 = d/v1 = d/10, the second half t2 = d/40. Average speed is total distance divided by total time: v_avg = 2d / (d/10 + d/40) = 2 / (1/10 + 1/40) = 2 / (5/40) = 80/5 = 16 mi/hr. This is the harmonic mean of the two speeds, not the arithmetic mean, because the time spent at each speed differs.\n\nAnswer: (A)"
    },
